      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The main understandability issue is that `testRule1()` packs all six test pairs onto a single line, making the rule-to-input/expected mapping invisible. I'll reformat each pair onto its own line with an inline comment showing the rule, and improve the Javadoc.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `testRule1()` now places each input/expected pair on its own line with an inline comment identifying the specific transcoding rule, and the Javadoc enumerates all six transformations explicitly — making the intent of each case immediately clear without changing any test behaviour."
